  "Question": "If \\((m+1)+(n-1)i=0\\), what is \\(m\\)?",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "-1",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "If \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are real, \\(0=0+0i\\), so the real part satisfies \\(m+1=0\\), giving \\(m=-1\\).\n\nThe question does not specify that \\(m\\) and \\(n\\) are real, so the displayed coefficients cannot generally be treated as real and imaginary parts. If complex values are permitted, \\((m,n)=(-1,1)\\) satisfies the equation, but so does \\((m,n)=(0,1+i)\\), since\n\\[\n(0+1)+((1+i)-1)i=1+i^2=0.\n\\]\nThus the keyed value is \\(m=-1\\) under the real-number assumption, while the question as written has no unique answer.",
